concept :the_season_credit do
  name "The Season Credit"
  tags :biotech, :legibility, :ecology, :trade
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    What lets four days of tracing stand for a winter. #{ref :xincheng_yard, "The Xincheng yard"} can hold a bed against a hedge for four days and has no way to hold one against a season, and the difference is the whole of what a card does not cover. A credit closes it by arithmetic: for one class of strain, a figure saying how much of a season a four-day trace accounts for, established by running both readings on the same strain in the same year.

    The long half of the pairing is bought, not built. A sealed set goes up to #{ref :thorong_cold_house, "the Thorong cold house"} in the autumn carry and comes down at the melt, and what it cost was two carries and the season's rate.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "How A Credit Is Made"
    Two readings, one year, one strain. A bed reaching the end of its cycle is traced at five metres for four days under #{ref :the_seam_pass, "the procedure"} and broken; a sealed set of the same strain from the same bed goes up the pass and is read at the melt against its withheld tubes and its blanks.

    The figure written is the ratio between them, and it is written against the class rather than against the strain: what substrate the bed was grown on, how the network was pruned, how many cycles the lineage has run. A credit names the class, the year, the pass and the winter it was read in. It does not name a lineage, and a lineage crossing on a credit is crossing on somebody else's set.

    A card renewed under a credit says so on its face, with the class and the year. A card without that line means four days at five metres and nothing further, which is what most cards mean.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "The Pass Is Not The Same Winter Twice"
    A ratio read against a mild winter overstates every card renewed under it, so a reference set goes up with the paired sets every autumn: #{ref :gate_moss, "gate-moss"} off a crossing bed, the one organism both traditions handle without argument, racked in the same room and read the same morning. Its reading fixes the severity of that winter, and every credit computed that year is computed beside it. The readings sit in #{ref :the_thorong_book, "the house's book"}, one line to a set, in the only copy there is.

    Credits are re-established on a stated count of cycles rather than on a count of years, because a lineage run hard through a season has done more to itself than the calendar shows. #{ref :the_borrowed_season, "The Borrowed Season"} is the case that put the class line on the form, and after it a credit read against one substrate stopped travelling to another.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :trade, heading: "Glass Is Not A Planting"
    The #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeepers"} pay the Thorong carry out of the same villages below the pass and at the same rate, on the carrier's word, including for a set abandoned in shelter. Nothing else passes between them and the Holds. There is no agreement, no standing party, and no clerk on either side who has met one on the other.

    Gatekeeper samples remain sealed and travel alone in their cases, with no monastery specimens beside them. A set that arrives warm says nothing and is discarded.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — Semi-adjacent pull: the correlation of accelerated weathering to natural outdoor exposure. A short apparatus test substitutes for real-time exposure only where an acceleration factor has been established by running both on the same material, the factor belongs to the material class and is not transferable across classes, a control specimen is exposed alongside every cycle because the reference site's own severity varies year to year, and the factor is restated on interval. Borrowed: the paired reading, the class-not-article rule, the reference set fixing the winter, and re-establishment counted in cycles. Reason: it connects a four-day challenge regime to a one-season register regime without either party governing the other — the yard buys a season it cannot run, and the pass sells nothing but the winter it already has."
end
